Search the web for more on the book if you don't already have the details, passing focus: "books".

Present it properly: the title and author, a short line on what it's about, and why it fits what they said — the mood, the seed book, or the taste they described. Mention if it's part of a series.

Offer to help them get hold of it, anchored in how they already read (their store, app, or library) rather than defaulting to a generic retailer. If that preference isn't known yet, ask once and save it with add_knowledge so future picks don't need to ask again.

If anything durable about their taste came up along the way — a genre or author they love, something they said they're avoiding — and it isn't already known, save it with add_knowledge so future picks don't need to ask again. The specific book chosen isn't worth noting on its own; it's the preferences behind it that are useful later.

Once it's presented, call advance_flow to finish.
